:: Mansion Gym Bar Intro
<<endevent>><<npc "Avery">><<person1>><<speechresolve>>
<<if $speech_attitude_avery>>
	<<set _speechAttitudeResolved to "meek">>
<</if>>
Avery
<<if $averyragerevealed is 1 and C.npc.Avery.rage gte 40>>
	puts <<his>> glass down hard against the table, then gets to <<his>> feet.
<<else>>
	puts <<his>> glass down and gets to <<his>> feet.
<</if>>
<<He>> adjusts <<his>> cuffs, then crosses the lounge to the door in the far corner.
You'd taken it for a store cupboard, and never had a reason to open it.
<br><br>
"You've only seen the parts of this house I've had cause to show you," <<he>> says, resting <<his>> hand on the handle.
"There are two more rooms you haven't seen."
<br><br>
<<He>> opens the door, then moves aside to let you enter.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Mansion Gym Bar Intro Gym]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Mansion Gym Bar Intro Gym
<<effects>>
You step into a small gym. A bench and a rack of weights take up one side of the room, while a treadmill faces the window.
A heavy bag hangs in the corner, with a long mirror fixed to the wall opposite it.
<br><br>
"A gym," Avery says as <<he>> follows you inside. "You spend enough time travelling into town to train.
I thought it would be more convenient to have somewhere here as well."
<br><br>
<<He>> walks over to the weight rack and picks up one of the smaller dumbbells.
<<He>> tests its weight in one hand before putting it back exactly where it was.
<<if $averyragerevealed is 1 and C.npc.Avery.rage gte 40>>
    "I paid a great deal for all of this," <<he>> says, looking over the room. "Take care of it."
<<else>>
    "I paid a great deal for all of this," <<he>> says. "Though I doubt that surprises you."
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Thank <<him>>|Mansion Gym Bar Intro Bar]]>><<set $phase to 1>><<npcincr Avery love 1>><</link>><<glove>>
<br>
<<link [[Ask why <<he>> did this now|Mansion Gym Bar Intro Bar]]>><<set $phase to 2>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Say nothing|Mansion Gym Bar Intro Bar]]>><<set $phase to 3>><</link>>
<br>

:: Mansion Gym Bar Intro Bar
<<effects>><<speechresolve>>
<<if $speech_attitude_avery>>
	<<set _speechAttitudeResolved to "meek">>
<</if>>
<<if $phase is 1>>
	<<if _speechAttitudeResolved is "meek">>
		"Th-Thank you," you say. "For letting me use the gym too."
	<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy">>
		"Thank you," you say, looking at the floor. "For letting me use it."
	<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
		"Thank you," you say. "It's kind of you to let me use the gym as well."
	<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
		"Thank you," you say. "I'll take good care of the equipment."
	<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
		"Thanks," you say. "I'll definitely make use of it."
	<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
		"Not bad," you say. "I suppose I'll use it."
	<<else>>
		"Thank you," you say. "I didn't expect you to let me use it too."
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	Avery waves away your thanks. "It's just a room. You don't need to make such a fuss about it."
<<elseif $phase is 2>>
	<<if _speechAttitudeResolved is "meek">>
		"Why now?" you ask. "I mean, after all this time."
	<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy">>
		"Why now?" you ask. "The rooms were here before."
	<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
		"May I ask why now?" you say. "The rooms have been empty a long while."
	<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
		"Why now?" you ask. "You've had the space for years."
	<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
		"Why now?" you ask. "You've sat on these rooms for years."
	<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
		"What changed?" you ask. "You've had these rooms the whole time."
	<<else>>
		"Why now?" you ask. "You've had the space all along."
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	Avery keeps one hand on the door handle while <<he>> looks at you. "Because you're living here, and you'll go on living here.
    A house should fit the people in it." <<He>> turns for the door. "Don't read more into it than that."
<<else>>
	You don't say anything. Avery waits for an answer, then turns for the door when none comes.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<He>> leads you back out through the lounge and into the dining room. Past the end of the table stands a
tall cabinet you've walked by a hundred times without once opening. <<He>> opens both of its doors at once.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Mansion Gym Bar Intro Bar 2]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Mansion Gym Bar Intro Bar 2
<<effects>>
Bottles are arranged by type. Beer and cider are on the bottom shelf, stronger drinks are on the middle shelf,
and wine is stored along the top.
"And this," Avery says, opening the cabinet wider. "I keep it stocked. You may drink from it."
<br><br>
<<He>> looks over the shelves before turning back to you.
<<if $averyragerevealed is 1 and C.npc.Avery.rage gte 40>>
	"Conditions. Three drinks in a day."
<<else>>
	"With conditions. Three drinks in a day."
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<He>> taps the middle shelf twice. "I know how much I keep here. If I come home and find half of it gone,
we'll be having a different conversation."
<br><br>
<<He>> reaches inside and straightens one of the bottles before continuing.
"Second condition. You can use the gym and drink from here while I'm out. Not while I'm home."
<br><br>
<<link [[Agree|Mansion Gym Bar Intro End]]>><<set $phase2 to 1>><<npcincr Avery dom 1>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Ask what happens if <<he>> finds out|Mansion Gym Bar Intro End]]>><<set $phase2 to 2>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Point out that it's <<his>> house either way|Mansion Gym Bar Intro End]]>><<set $phase2 to 3>><<npcincr Avery rage 1>><</link>>
<br>

:: Mansion Gym Bar Intro End
<<effects>><<set $avery_mansion.gym_bar_intro to true>><<speechresolve>>
<<if $speech_attitude_avery>>
    <<set _speechAttitudeResolved to "meek">>
<</if>>
<<if $phase2 is 1>>
    <<if _speechAttitudeResolved is "meek">>
        "I understand," you say. "I can only use them while you're out."
     <<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
        "Fine," you say. "Gym and drinks only when you're out. Got it."
    <<else>>
         "Understood," you say. "I can only use them while you're out."
    <</if>>
    <br><br>
    "Good," Avery says with a small smile.<<gdom>>
<<elseif $phase2 is 2>>
    "What happens if I use the gym or take a drink while you're home?" you ask.
    <br><br>
    <<if $averyragerevealed is 1 and C.npc.Avery.rage gte 40>>
         "I'd make sure you didn't do it again," <<he>> says.
    <<else>>
          "I'd remind you of the rule," <<he>> says. "I expect you to follow it."
    <</if>>
<<else>>
    "You own the house whether you're here or not," you say. "Why does it matter?"
    <br><br>
    "Because when I'm home, I want your attention," Avery says. "Use the gym or have a drink while I'm out.
    I don't want to come home and find you running on the treadmill or sitting here with my scotch."<<garage>>
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<He>> closes the cabinet and walks towards the lounge. At the doorway, <<he>> stops and looks back at you.
<br><br>
"One more thing. Don't tell me every time you use them.
<<if $averyragerevealed is 1 and C.npc.Avery.rage gte 40>>
    No announcements. Don't thank me again either. If I'm out, I don't need to hear what you did while I was gone."
<<else>>
    No announcements, and don't thank me again," <<he>> says. "Use what I've allowed you to use,
    put everything back afterwards, and leave it at that."
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<He>> keeps looking at you until you nod. Satisfied, <<he>> turns away and returns to the lounge.
You follow <<him>> inside, where <<he>> sits back down in <<his>> chair.
<br><br>
<span class="gold">Avery has shown you the home gym and private bar.</span>
<br><br>
<<endevent>>
<<avery_mansion_end_links>>

:: Mansion Gym
<<set $location to "avery_mansion">><<effects>><<avery_mansion>>
<<if !$avery_mansion.gym_bar_intro or !["away", "work"].includes($avery_mansion.schedule)>>
	You have no business being in here right now.
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Go back|Mansion Lounge]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
    You open the door in the corner of the lounge and step into the gym.
    <br>
    A bench and weight rack stand against one wall, with a treadmill by the window and a heavy bag in the corner.
    It is smaller than the gym in town, but you can use everything here while Avery is away.
	<br><br>
	<<if $leftarm is "bound" or $rightarm is "bound">>
		<span class="blue">You can't use any of this with your hands bound.</span>
		<br>
	<<elseif $exposed gte 1>>
		<<covered>>
		<br>
	<<else>>
		<<icon "physique.png">><<link [[Lift weights (0:30)|Mansion Gym Weights]]>><<pass 30>><</link>><<gphysique>><<gathletics>><<note " Moderate fatigue" "red">>
		<br>
		<<icon "physique.png">><<link [[Use the treadmill (0:30)|Mansion Gym Cardio]]>><<pass 30>><</link>><<gathletics>><<gwillpower>><<note " Moderate fatigue" "red">>
		<br>
		<<if $combatExtended.standingFights is 1 and $combatExtended.footworkToggle is 1>>
			<<icon "physique.png">><<link [[Practise footwork (0:30)|Mansion Gym Footwork]]>><<pass 30>><</link>><<gfootwork>><<note " Moderate fatigue" "red">>
			<br>
		<</if>>
		<<if $combatExtended.strikingToggle is 1>>
			<<icon "physique.png">><<link [[Punch the heavy bag (0:30)|Mansion Gym Striking]]>><<pass 30>><</link>><<gstriking>><<note " Moderate fatigue" "red">>
			<br>
		<</if>>
		<<if $combatExtended.kickingToggle is 1>>
			<<icon "physique.png">><<link [[Kick the heavy bag (0:30)|Mansion Gym Kicking]]>><<pass 30>><</link>><<gkicking>><<note " Moderate fatigue" "red">>
			<br>
		<</if>>
	<</if>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Head back to the lounge|Mansion Lounge]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>
<br>

:: Mansion Gym Weights
<<effects>><<avery_mansion>>
<<if !["away", "work"].includes($avery_mansion.schedule)>>
    <<avery_gym_caught>>
<<else>>
    You add weights to the bar and lie back on the bench. The first set feels easy enough,
    so you add another plate before starting again.
    <br><br>
    The extra weight slows you down. Near the end of the second set, your arms begin to shake.
    You pause between each rep, taking a breath before forcing the bar up again.
    <br><br>
    You manage one last rep and push the bar back onto the rack. Your arms drop to your sides as you lie there,
    breathing heavily until they stop shaking.
    <br><br>
    When you finally sit up, your shirt is damp with sweat and sticking to your back.
    <<physique 1>><<gphysique>><<athletics 1>><<gathletics>><<tiredness 6>><<ggtiredness>><<stress 3>><<gstress>>
    <br><br>
    <<link [[Next|Mansion Gym]]>><</link>>
    <br>
<</if>>

:: Mansion Gym Cardio
<<effects>><<avery_mansion>>
<<if !["away", "work"].includes($avery_mansion.schedule)>>
    <<avery_gym_caught>>
<<else>>
    You step onto the treadmill and start at an easy pace. As you walk,
    you look through the window at the garden and let your body warm up.
    <br><br>
    After a while, you increase the speed. Your breathing grows heavier as you keep moving,
    and your calves begin to ache. You resist the urge to slow down and keep going until the timer reaches zero.
    <br><br>
    You lower the speed until the belt stops, then hold the handrail while you catch your breath.
    <<athletics 1>><<gathletics>><<willpower 1>><<gwillpower>><<tiredness 6>><<ggtiredness>><<stress 3>><<gstress>>
    <br><br>
    <<link [[Next|Mansion Gym]]>><</link>>
    <br>
<</if>>

:: Mansion Gym Footwork
<<effects>><<avery_mansion>>
<<if !["away", "work"].includes($avery_mansion.schedule)>>
    <<avery_gym_caught>>
<<else>>
    You stand in front of the mirror and begin with a simple step pattern, moving forwards,
    backwards, then from side to side. Whenever your feet cross, you stop and correct them before starting again.
    <br><br>
    After a few tries, the movement starts to feel easier. You increase the pace, but your first quick
    turns throw you off balance. You slow down, keep your weight centred, then try again.
    <br><br>
    You repeat the drill until you can change direction without stumbling or leaning back.
    By the time you stop, your legs are sore from keeping your knees bent.
    <<footwork 1>><<gfootwork>><<athletics 1>><<gathletics>><<tiredness 6>><<ggtiredness>><<stress 3>><<gstress>>
    <br><br>
    <<link [[Next|Mansion Gym]]>><</link>>
    <br>
<</if>>

:: Mansion Gym Striking
<<effects>><<avery_mansion>>
<<if !["away", "work"].includes($avery_mansion.schedule)>>
    <<avery_gym_caught>>
<<else>>
    You stand in front of the punching bag and throw a few slow punches,
    letting it swing back towards you before hitting it again.
    <br><br>
    You pick up the pace and start throwing short combinations. A few punches land badly and send
    pain through your wrist, so you adjust your stance and put more of your body behind each hit.
    <br><br>
    You continue until your arms start to feel heavy. After one last punch, you catch the swinging bag with
    both hands and hold it still before stepping back. Your knuckles are red from the training.
    <<striking 1>><<gstriking>><<physique 1>><<gphysique>><<tiredness 6>><<ggtiredness>><<stress 3>><<gstress>>
    <br><br>
    <<link [[Next|Mansion Gym]]>><</link>>
    <br>
<</if>>

:: Mansion Gym Kicking
<<effects>><<avery_mansion>>
<<if !["away", "work"].includes($avery_mansion.schedule)>>
    <<avery_gym_caught>>
<<else>>
    You begin with low kicks, striking the bottom of the bag while turning your other foot with each hit.
    The bag swings a little more as you settle into the movement.
    <br><br>
    You try kicking higher, but your first kick at chest height throws you off balance.
    You grab the support beside the bag before you fall, then lower your aim and keep practising.
    <br><br>
    After several more attempts, you manage a higher kick without stumbling.
    <br><br>
    Your shin aches from the hits, while the leg supporting your weight feels stiff.
    You lean against the wall and stretch it before heading back.
    <<kicking 1>><<gkicking>><<physique 1>><<gphysique>><<tiredness 6>><<ggtiredness>><<stress 3>><<gstress>>
    <br><br>
    <<link [[Next|Mansion Gym]]>><</link>>
    <br>
<</if>>

:: Mansion Bar
<<set $location to "avery_mansion">><<effects>><<avery_mansion>>
<<if !$avery_mansion.gym_bar_intro or !["away", "work"].includes($avery_mansion.schedule)>>
    You shouldn't be in here while Avery is home.
    <br><br>
    <<link [[Go back|Mansion Dining]]>><</link>>
    <br>
<<else>>
    <<if typeof $daily.avery.bar_drinks isnot "number" or Number.isNaN($daily.avery.bar_drinks)>>
        <<set $daily.avery.bar_drinks to 0>>
    <</if>>
    <<if !Array.isArray($avery_mansion.bar_tried)>><<set $avery_mansion.bar_tried to []>><</if>>
    You open the tall cabinet at the far end of the dining table. Beer and cider are kept on the bottom shelf,
    with bottles of spirits above them and wine stored at the top.
    <br><br>
    <<if playerIsPregnant() and playerAwareTheyArePregnant()>>
        You look over the bottles, but close the cabinet again.
        <span class="blue">You know you're pregnant, so drinking now doesn't feel right.</span>
        <br><br>
        <<link [[Go back|Mansion Dining]]>><</link>>
        <br>
    <<else>>
        <<if $daily.avery.bar_drinks gte 3>>
            You've already had <<= $daily.avery.bar_drinks>> drinks today.
            <span class="red">If you take any more, Avery may notice that some of the bottles are getting low.</span>
            <br><br>
        <</if>>
        <<foodicon "beer">><<link [[Pour a beer|Mansion Bar Drink]]>><<set $phase to "beer">><</link>>
        <br>
        <<foodicon "cider">><<link [[Pour a cider|Mansion Bar Drink]]>><<set $phase to "cider">><</link>>
        <br>
        <<foodicon "whisky">><<link [[Pour a bourbon|Mansion Bar Drink]]>><<set $phase to "bourbon">><</link>>
        <br>
        <<foodicon "scotch">><<link [[Pour a scotch|Mansion Bar Drink]]>><<set $phase to "scotch">><</link>>
        <br>
        <<foodicon "brandy">><<link [[Pour a brandy|Mansion Bar Drink]]>><<set $phase to "brandy">><</link>>
        <br>
        <<foodicon "gin">><<link [[Pour a gin|Mansion Bar Drink]]>><<set $phase to "gin">><</link>>
        <br>
        <<foodicon "vodka">><<link [[Pour a vodka|Mansion Bar Drink]]>><<set $phase to "vodka">><</link>>
        <br>
        <<foodstufficon "red_wine">><<link [[Pour a red wine|Mansion Bar Drink]]>><<set $phase to "red">><</link>>
        <br>
        <<foodstufficon "white_wine">><<link [[Pour a white wine|Mansion Bar Drink]]>><<set $phase to "white">><</link>>
        <br><br>
        <<link [[Close the cabinet and leave|Mansion Dining]]>><</link>>
        <br>
    <</if>>
<</if>>

:: Mansion Bar Drink
<<effects>><<avery_mansion>>
<<if !["away", "work"].includes($avery_mansion.schedule)>>
	You hear Avery moving somewhere in the house. You quickly put the bottle back and
    close the cabinet before <<nnpc_he "Avery">> comes in and finds you drinking.
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Mansion Dining]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	<<if !Array.isArray($avery_mansion.bar_tried)>><<set $avery_mansion.bar_tried to []>><</if>>
	<<set _first to !$avery_mansion.bar_tried.includes($phase)>>
	<<run $avery_mansion.bar_tried.pushUnique($phase)>>
	<<set $daily.avery.bar_drinks += 1>>
	<<switch $phase>>
		<<case "beer">>
			<<wearProp "beer bottle">>
			You take a bottle from the bottom shelf and open it. The beer is cold and bitter,
            making you pause after the first mouthful.
			<br><br>
			<<if _first>>
				It tastes better than the beer served at the pub in town. You look at the bottle
                again before taking another drink.
			<<else>>
				You stay by the cabinet and drink straight from the bottle.
			<</if>>
		<<case "cider">>
			<<wearProp "cider">>
			You pour yourself a glass of cider. It is sweet and easy to drink,
            though the alcohol becomes more noticeable after a few mouthfuls.
			<br><br>
			<<if _first>>
				You turn the bottle around to read the label. You have never seen the brand in any of the shops in town.
			<<else>>
				You finish the rest in a few long drinks.
			<</if>>
		<<case "bourbon">>
			<<wearProp "whisky">>
			You pour a measure of bourbon and take a drink. It tastes sweeter than you expected,
            followed by a strong warmth in your throat and chest.
			<br><br>
			<<if _first>>
				This is the only open bottle on the shelf. There is only about a third left,
                with another unopened bottle behind it.<span class="gold"> It seems to be Avery's usual choice.</span>
			<<else>>
				You take another drink, slower this time.
			<</if>>
            <<trauma -2>><<ltrauma>>
		<<case "scotch">>
			<<wearProp "scotch">>
			You pour a measure of scotch and take a sip. The taste is strong, with a smoky flavour
            that stays in your mouth afterwards.
			<br><br>
			<<if _first>>
				You check the label. The name of the distillery is difficult to pronounce,
                and the year printed on the bottle is older than you are.
			<<else>>
				You continue drinking, taking smaller sips.
			<</if>>
		<<case "brandy">>
			<<wearProp "brandy">>
			You pour a small glass of brandy and take a sip. It is sweet and strong, warming your throat as you swallow.
			<br><br>
			<<if _first>>
				You look at the glass. You have mostly seen people drink brandy like this in films.
			<<else>>
				You take your time finishing it.
			<</if>>
		<<case "gin">>
			You pour a measure of gin and drink it without mixing anything in. The strong, bitter taste makes you pull a face.
			<br><br>
			<<if _first>>
				You spot some tonic in the cabinet below and decide that would probably make it easier to drink next time.
			<<else>>
				You breathe out through your mouth, trying to clear the taste.
			<</if>>
		<<case "vodka">>
			<<wearProp "vodka">>
			You pour a shot of vodka and swallow it in one go. There is little taste at first,
            but the alcohol burns your throat a second later.
			<br><br>
			<<if _first>>
				You put the glass down and understand why most people mix it with something.
			<<else>>
				You blink away the tears in your eyes before setting the glass down.
			<</if>>
		<<case "red">>
			<<wearProp "red wine">>
			You take a bottle from the rack and pour a glass of red wine. It is dry and less sweet than you expected.
			<br><br>
			<<if _first>>
				You take another sip, then another. The taste becomes easier to enjoy once you know what to expect.
			<<else>>
				You sit on the arm of a nearby chair and drink it slowly.
			<</if>>
		<<case "white">>
			<<wearProp "white wine">>
			You pour a glass of chilled white wine. It has a light, sharp taste and goes down more easily than the red.
			<br><br>
			<<if _first>>
				You take a few more sips and soon realise the glass is nearly empty.
			<<else>>
				You stay beside the cabinet and drink it slowly.
			<</if>>
	<</switch>>
	<<switch $phase>>
		<<case "beer" "cider">>
			<<drunk 80>>
		<<case "gin" "vodka" "bourbon" "scotch" "brandy">>
			<<drunk 160>>
		<<case "red" "white">>
			<<drunk 120>>
	<</switch>>
	<<gdrunk>>
    <br><br>
	You set the drink down and loosen your grip on the glass. The tightness in your shoulders eases.<<stress -6>><<llstress>>
	<br><br>
	<<if $daily.avery.bar_drinks gte 4>>
		<span class="red">You have had more than Avery allowed. If <<nnpc_he "Avery">> checks the bottles,
        <<nnpc_he "Avery">> may notice some are emptier than they should be.</span>
		<<if $avery_mansion>><<set $avery_mansion.rage.bar_overdrink to true>><</if>>
		<br><br>
	<<elseif $daily.avery.bar_drinks is 3>>
		<span class="blue">That is your third drink today. Avery told you not to have any more.</span>
		<br><br>
	<</if>>
	<<link [[Next|Mansion Bar]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>

/* GARDEN */
:: Mansion Garden Crops Intro
<<set $location to "avery_mansion">><<set $bus to "avery_garden">><<set $outside to 1>><<effects>>
<<endevent>>
<<npc Avery>><<person1>>
You find Avery standing among the flowerbeds with <<his>> hands clasped behind <<his>> back.
<<He>> is watching a bee work its way along a row of flowers, and doesn't look up as you come along the path.
<br><br>
When <<he>> does, <<he>> straightens, and the distant look gives way to a careful smile.
"<<pcpetname "Avery">>," <<he>> says. "I didn't hear you."
<br><br>
<<He>> turns back to the garden. "I've been spending more time out here lately. Strange, isn't it?
I never used to. There was always something more pressing." <<He>> frowns.
"Funny, how that changes, when you nearly don't get the chance to do anything at all."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Mansion Garden Crops Intro 2]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Mansion Garden Crops Intro 2
<<effects>>
Avery falls quiet. You recognise the look on <<his>> face. <<He>> is grateful, though too proud to say it properly.
You pulled <<him>> back from the edge, and <<he>> has never been good at admitting when <<he>> needed help.
<br><br>
"You saved me," <<he>> says at last, still looking at the path. "I don't think I've properly thanked you for that.
I'm not... entirely certain I know how." <<He>> turns <<his>> cufflink over between two fingers, then lets <<his>> hand drop and looks back at you.
<br><br>
"So let me try it like this." <<He>> nods towards a sheltered corner of the garden, where glass panels stand
over a patch of bare, turned soil. "That's yours, if you want it. Grow whatever you like in it.
Nobody else will put a hand on it. Somewhere in this house that belongs to you, and it's here, with me."
<br><br>
<<link [[Accept|Mansion Garden Crops Accept]]>><<set $avery_mansion.crops to 1>><<set $monthly.averyGardenPlot to true>><<run ["turnip", "cabbage", "potato"].forEach(seed => $plants_known.pushUnique(seed))>><<npcincr Avery love 1>><<npcincr Avery rage -1>><</link>><<glove>><<larage>>
<br>
<<link [[Decline|Mansion Garden Crops Decline]]>><<set $avery_mansion.crops to 1>><<set $monthly.averyGardenPlot to true>><<run ["turnip", "cabbage", "potato"].forEach(seed => $plants_known.pushUnique(seed))>><</link>>
<br>

:: Mansion Garden Crops Accept
<<effects>>
You tell Avery you'd love nothing more.
<br><br>
Avery lets out a breath and <<his>> shoulders come down. "Good," <<he>> says. "Good."
<<He>> clears <<his>> throat and straightens up. "I'll have seeds and tools brought down this afternoon.
Turnip, cabbage, and potato to begin with, since none of them will punish you for a mistake.
The glass keeps it warm enough to grow all year round. I won't have your work ruined by the weather."
<br><br>
<<He>> turns towards the house, but before taking a step, <<he>> leans in and presses a kiss to your forehead.
"Enjoy it, <<pcpetname "Avery">>. Truly."
<br><br>
With that, <<he>> heads back towards the house, leaving you alone with your new patch of earth.
<br><br>
<span class="gold">You can now grow your own crops in Avery's garden, sheltered beneath glass so they thrive in any season.</span>
<br>
<<gardenicon "flower">><<link [[Tend the soil|Mansion Garden Plots]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave|Mansion Garden]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Mansion Garden Crops Decline
<<effects>>
You thank Avery, but tell <<him>> you couldn't possibly.
<br><br>
<<He>> only smiles and shakes <<his>> head. "It's already done, <<pcpetname "Avery">>.
The soil is turned, the glass is up. I'll not have it pulled apart again." <<He>> lowers <<his>> voice.
"Use it or don't, as you please. It isn't going anywhere."
<br><br>
"The seeds are already bought, so they'll be sent down with the tools. Turnip, cabbage, and potato."
<<He>> opens <<his>> mouth to add something, then shakes <<his>> head and turns towards the house. "I'll be inside."
<br><br>
<span class="gold">The patch is yours whenever you want it, sheltered beneath glass so it can be worked in any season.</span>
<br>
<<link [[Next|Mansion Garden]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Mansion Garden Whine
<<set $location to "avery_mansion">><<set $bus to "avery_garden">><<set $outside to 1>><<effects>>
<<endevent>>
<<npc Avery>><<person1>>
You crouch by the plot, frowning at the state of it. Half the beds have dried out again, and there's nowhere left to put anything new.
<br><br>
<<speechresolve>>
<<if $speech_attitude_avery>>
	<<set _speechAttitudeResolved to "meek">>
<</if>>
<<if _speechAttitudeResolved is "meek">>
	"Um... Avery?" you say, not quite looking up. "The plot's a bit small. And I can't always get to everything before it dries out."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy">>
	You rub the dirt from your fingertips before looking up. "Avery? Could we make the plot a bit bigger? I keep running out of room, and some of it dries before I get back to it."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
	You straighten the edge of the nearest bed with your hand. "Avery, could you have someone look at this? I can't keep all of it watered, and there's no room left."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "polite">>
	"Avery, could I ask you to have the plot expanded?" you say. "I'm short on space, and the watering takes longer than I can manage."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant">>
	You spread your hands over the cramped beds. "Avery, look at this. My grand agricultural empire has already run out of land. I need more room, and something better for the watering."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
	"This is pathetic," you announce, not bothering to look up. "Half of it's dried to dust and there's no room for anything else. Fix it."
<<else>>
	"Avery," you say, straightening up. "The plot's too small, and I can't keep on top of the watering. It needs sorting."
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<if C.npc.Avery.rage gte 60>>
	Avery's jaw tightens. <<He>> looks from you to the dry beds, then exhales through <<his>> nose.
	<br><br>
	"Is that so? Very well, I'll have it seen to. Try to sound grateful next time."
	<<He>> walks off before you can answer.<<npcincr Avery rage 1>><<larage>>
<<elseif C.npc.Avery.love gte 40 and C.npc.Avery.love gt C.npc.Avery.rage>>
	Avery crosses to the plot and crouches beside you. <<He>> presses two fingers into the dry soil and rubs the dirt between them.
	<br><br>
	"Oh, <<pcpetname "Avery">>, why didn't you say something sooner?" <<He>> wipes the dirt from your fingers, then keeps hold of your hand.
	"Leave it with me. I'll have it done properly. You deserve better than this."<<npcincr Avery love 1>><<glove>>
<<elseif C.npc.Avery.rage gte 25>>
	Avery looks over the cramped beds, then brushes the dirt from <<his>> hands.
	"Fine," <<he>> says, brushing off <<his>> hands. "I'll get someone on it. Try not to let the rest die in the meantime."
<<else>>
	Avery turns from the nearby flowerbed and looks over the cramped plot.
	"Hmmn. Fair enough," <<he>> says, considering the cramped little plot. "I'll have it expanded. Shouldn't take long."
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<set $avery_mansion.crops_upgrade to 1>><<set $weekly.averyGardenUpgrade to true>>
<span class="gold">Avery will have the garden sorted out within the week.</span>
<br>
<<link [[Next|Mansion Garden]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Mansion Garden Plots
<<set $location to "avery_mansion">><<set $bus to "avery_garden">><<set $outside to 0>><<effects>>
<<if !$plots["avery_mansion"]>>
	<<plots_init avery_mansion 3 earth 3 medium>>
<</if>>
<<if $avery_mansion.crops_upgrade is 1 and !$weekly.averyGardenUpgrade>>
	<<set $avery_mansion.crops_upgrade to 3>>
	<<set $avery_mansion.greenhouse to true>>
	<<add_plot avery_mansion earth 3 medium>>
	<<add_plot avery_mansion earth 3 medium>>
	<<add_plot avery_mansion earth 3 medium>>
	True to <<nnpc_his "Avery">> word, Avery's had the plot seen to. The bed's been widened, fresh soil turned into three new rows,
	and a narrow pipe now runs along the back wall, dripping into the earth below.
	<br><br>
<</if>>
<<if $avery_mansion.schedule is "garden" and !$daily.avery.gardenPlant and $plots["avery_mansion"].every(plot => plot.stage is 0)>>
	<<set $daily.avery.gardenPlant to true>>
	<<set _averySeeds to Object.entries(setup.foodstuff)
		.filter(seed => seed[1].tending?.has_seeds and seed[1].tending.planting_bed is "earth" and seed[1].tending.seasons?.includes(Time.season))
		.sort((a, b) => b[1].shop.sell_price - a[1].shop.sell_price)
		.slice(0, 5)>>
	<<set $avery_mansion.plant_together to weightedRandom.apply(null, _averySeeds.map(seed => [seed[0], 1]))>>
	<<include "Mansion Garden Plant Together">>
<<else>>
	<<plot_effects>>
	You step into the glass-walled corner of the garden Avery set aside for you.
	The air inside is warm, and sunlight falls across the soil through the glass.
	<span class="gold">Plants can be grown here at any time of year.</span>
	<br><br>
	<<display_plot avery_mansion>>
	<br>
	<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave|Mansion Garden]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>

:: Mansion Garden Plant Together
<<effects>><<endevent>><<set _plant to setup.foodstuff[$avery_mansion.plant_together]>>
<<npc Avery>><<person1>>
You open the glass door and enter the garden room. As you walk towards the tools, the door closes behind you.
<br><br>
You turn around and see Avery carrying a shallow wooden box under one arm.
<<He>> walks over to the empty planting bed and looks down at the soil.
"You still haven't planted anything?"
<br><br>
Before you can answer, Avery puts the box down and kneels beside the bed.
"I gave you this space to grow something, <<pcpetname "Avery">>. I'm not leaving it empty."
<br><br>
<<He>> opens the box. Inside are two pairs of gardening gloves, a small trowel,
and a packet marked <span class="gold"><<print _plant.name>></span>.
"I had several things brought over," <<he>> says, picking up the packet. "I chose this one for you."
<br><br>
<<He>> holds it out so you can see the label.
"Come here. We're planting it."
<br><br>
<<link [[Plant the garden together|Mansion Garden Plant Together 1]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Refuse|Mansion Garden Plant Together Refuse]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Mansion Garden Plant Together 1
<<set $location to "avery_mansion">><<set $bus to "avery_garden">><<set $outside to 0>><<effects>>
<<if $speech_attitude_avery>>
	You glance at the empty bed, then at the spare gloves in Avery's hand.
	"O-okay," you say. "If you want to do it together."
<<else>>
	<<switch $speech_attitude>>
		<<case "docile">>
			You step closer and look over the seeds Avery brought.
			"Of course, Avery," you say. "Tell me where you want me to start."
		<<case "meek">>
			You take the spare gloves, turning them over in your hands.
			"O-okay," you say. "I'll try not to mess anything up."
		<<case "shy">>
			You look down at the seeds, surprised that Avery brought them <<himself>>.
			"You chose these?" you ask. "I... I'd like to plant them with you."
		<<case "polite">>
			You look over the tools and seeds Avery prepared.
			"Thank you for bringing everything," you say. "I'd be happy to plant them with you."
		<<case "confident">>
			You take the spare gloves from Avery and pull them on.
			"Good choice," you say. "Show me where you want to start."
		<<case "bratty">>
			You take the gloves before Avery can put them down.
			"You mean <i>we're</i> planting them," you say. "I'm not doing all the work while you stand there."
		<<case "cruel">>
			You look from the seeds to the empty patch of soil.
			"You really bought all this because you didn't like an empty garden? Fine. Help me make it worth the trouble."
		<<case "flamboyant">>
			You take the gloves and gesture towards the empty bed.
			"Then we should do this properly," you say. "You picked the plants. I'll help give them a good start."
		<<case "special">>
			You pick up the gloves and look between Avery and the empty bed.
			"If we're both planting them, we should each take one side," you say. "Then we can see whose side grows better."
		<<case "capricious">>
			You eye the seeds for a few seconds before taking the gloves.
			"I was thinking of planting something else," you say. "But yours look better right now. Let's use them."
		<<case "fickle">>
			You pick up the gloves, still studying the seeds.
			"I might like them," you say. "Ask me again when they've actually grown."
		<<default>>
			You take the spare gloves from Avery.
			"All right," you say. "Let's plant them."
	<</switch>>
<</if>>
<br><br>
Avery watches you pull on the gloves, then gives a small nod. <<He>> picks up the seeds and walks towards the empty bed.
"Start from that end," <<he>> says. "I'll take this side."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Mansion Garden Plant Together 2]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Mansion Garden Plant Together 2
<<set $location to "avery_mansion">><<set $bus to "avery_garden">><<set $outside to 0>><<effects>>
<<set _plant to setup.foodstuff[$avery_mansion.plant_together]>><<pass 3>>
You kneel beside Avery. <<He>> pours a few <<print _plant.name>> seeds into <<his>> palm,
looking them over before choosing where to plant them.
<br><br>
<<switch $avery_mansion.plant_together>>
	<<case "cauliflower">>
		"Useful, easy to keep in order, and they don't take up too much room," <<he>> says.
		"I can think of worse things to grow."
	<<case "pink_rose">>
		Avery looks towards the roses outside. "Let's put the pink ones here.
		This part of the garden could use something a little softer."
	<<case "strange_flower">>
		The seeds have an unusual shape. Avery picks one up and turns it between <<his>> fingers.
		"The seller couldn't tell me what they'll grow into. They were expensive, so I hope the result is worth it."
	<<case "red_rose">>
		<<He>> looks towards the other rose beds. "Red will stand out more here.
		If we're planting roses, we may as well choose ones people will notice."
	<<case "white_rose">>
		Avery looks over the other roses outside. "White will look good beside all that colour.
		Simple, but difficult to ignore."
	<<case "orchid">>
		"Expensive and difficult to look after. They need plenty of attention."
		<<He>> notices the look you give <<him>>. "I know what you're thinking. Keep it to yourself."
	<<case "sunflower">>
		Avery points towards the part of the garden that gets the most sunlight.
		"They'll grow tallest over there. Let's give them enough room."
	<<case "plumeria">>
		"These weren't easy to find," <<he>> says, looking pleased with <<himself>>.
		"Since we're planting something together, I wanted something a little unusual."
	<<case "turnip">>
		Avery notices your expression. "Don't look at me like that.
		A garden doesn't need to be full of flowers. We can grow something useful too."
	<<case "pepper">>
		Avery smiles at you. "Peppers should make things a little more interesting.
		Just don't blame me when you eat one that's too hot."
	<<case "cabbage">>
		"Cabbage isn't exciting, but it's useful and easy enough to grow."
		<<He>> catches your surprised look.
		"What? I don't need everything in my garden to be expensive."
<</switch>>
<br><br>
Avery tips the seeds back into <<his>> hand and looks at you. "Come on. I'm not doing all the work myself."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Mansion Garden Plant Together 3]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Mansion Garden Plant Together 3
<<effects>><<pass 3>>
Avery works the trowel through the soil to loosen it again, then holds it out so you can do the same on your side.
You break up the last hard lumps between you and flatten the surface with your palms.
<br><br>
<<He>> takes the trowel back and drags its end along the bed, cutting a shallow line for the seeds.
<<He>> presses a mark into the soil every hand's width, then passes the trowel to you.
<br><br>
You start doing the same down your half of the row. When one of your marks sits too close to the last,
Avery reaches over and moves your hand a little further along.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Mansion Garden Plant Together 3.1]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Mansion Garden Plant Together 3.1
<<effects>><<pass 3>>
At first, Avery corrects nearly every hole you make. <<He>> points out where to dig, how deep to press the trowel,
and how much space to leave before the next seed. After several tries, <<he>> stops interrupting and works down <<his>> side of the row.
<br><br>
You settle into the same pace. When you finish with the trowel, Avery takes it from you and uses it on <<his>> side;
when <<he>> is done, <<he>> passes it back before you need to ask. You keep moving from one marked spot to the next.
<br><br>
By the time you reach the end of the row, your grip on the trowel has loosened. You stop glancing over at Avery
between each hole and keep working beside <<him>>.<<stress -6>><<llstress>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Mansion Garden Plant Together 3.2]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Mansion Garden Plant Together 3.2
<<set $location to "avery_mansion">><<set $bus to "avery_garden">><<set $outside to 0>><<effects>>
<<set _plant to setup.foodstuff[$avery_mansion.plant_together]>>
<<if C.npc.Avery.love gte 40 and C.npc.Avery.love gt C.npc.Avery.rage>>
	Avery reaches across to steady your hand as you press in the last mark. <<His>> fingers stay on yours
	after the mark is made. "Careful with them, <<pcpetname "Avery">>. I want to see how well these grow."
<<elseif C.npc.Avery.rage gte 60>>
	You press one of the holes too deep. Avery takes your wrist before you can move on.
	"Not that deep."
	<br><br>
	<<He>> lowers your hand and shows you how far to press into the soil, then lets go.
	"If we're doing this, we're doing it properly."
<<else>>
	Avery finishes <<his>> half of the row, sits back on <<his>> heels and looks along both sides of it.
	<<He>> moves one of your marks over with <<his>> thumb, then leaves the rest alone.
<</if>>
<br><br>
The row is marked from one end to the other. Avery opens the packet and shakes half the seeds into your palm.
<br><br>
<<link `"Plant the " + _plant.name + " seeds together (0:20)"` "Mansion Garden Plant Together 4">><</link>>
<br>

:: Mansion Garden Plant Together 4
<<set $location to "avery_mansion">><<set $bus to "avery_garden">><<set $outside to 0>><<effects>>
<<set _plant to setup.foodstuff[$avery_mansion.plant_together]>>
<<set _plantbed to $plots["avery_mansion"].find(plot => plot.stage is 0)>>
<<if _plantbed>>
	You start at one end of the empty row while Avery starts at the other. You make small holes in the soil
	and place a seed into each one. By the time you meet in the middle, the whole row is planted.
	<br><br>
	You cover the seeds with soil and press it down lightly.<<run plantSeedsInPlot(_plantbed, $avery_mansion.plant_together)>><<set _plantbed.water to 1>><<run $plants_known.pushUnique($avery_mansion.plant_together)>><<pass 20>><<tending 2>>
	<br><br>
	Avery waters the row while you gather the tools and put them back in the box. When you finish,
	<<he>> sets the watering can down beside it. "There," <<he>> says, looking over the row. "That should do."
	<br><br>
	<<He>> folds the packet over and pushes it into your hand. "There are plenty left. Sow the rest wherever you want them."
	<br><br>
	Neither of you goes for the door. You brush the loose soil off your gloves, and when you both reach for the box
	your sleeves touch. You stay where you are.<<trauma -3>><<ltrauma>>
	<br><br>
	<<He>> pulls off <<his>> gloves and works the dirt out from under one thumbnail. <<He>> looks down at the planted row
	and smiles, then catches you watching, clears <<his>> throat, and sets the gloves on top of the box.
	<br><br>
	<<His>> cheeks have gone slightly red.
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Kiss Avery|Mansion Garden Plant Together Kiss]]>><</link>><<kissvirginitywarning>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Leave Avery to the quiet|Mansion Garden Plant Together Leave]]>><</link>>
<<else>>
	Avery looks over the plots. Every space is already in use.
	"Looks like you've already planted everything? Good."
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Look over the plots|Mansion Garden Plots]]>><<run delete $avery_mansion.plant_together>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Leave|Mansion Garden]]>><<run delete $avery_mansion.plant_together>><<endevent>><</link>>
<</if>>
<br>

:: Mansion Garden Plant Together Refuse
<<set $location to "avery_mansion">><<set $bus to "avery_garden">><<set $outside to 0>>
<<effects>><<speechresolve>>
<<if $speech_attitude_avery>>
	<<set _speechAttitudeResolved to "meek">>
<</if>>
<<if _speechAttitudeResolved is "meek">>
	"I don't want to," you say, before <<he>> can set the box down. "Not today. Sorry."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy">>
	"I'd rather not," you say, looking at the box instead of at <<him>>. "Not right now."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
	"I'd rather leave it as it is," you say. "I'm sorry."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "polite">>
	"Thank you for bringing it all down," you say, "but I don't want to plant anything today."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant">>
	"A generous offer," you say, "and I'm turning it down. The soil can wait."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
	"No," you say. "You can put it back in the box."
<<else>>
	"No," you say. "I don't want to plant anything today."
<</if>>
<br><br>
Avery says nothing. <<He>> looks at you, then at the bed, and nods once.
"Suit yourself."
<br><br>
<<He>> picks the box back up, tucks it under <<his>> arm and carries it out through the glass door.
The bed is as empty as it was when you came in.
<br><br>
<<link [[Look over the plots|Mansion Garden Plots]]>><<run delete $avery_mansion.plant_together>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Leave|Mansion Garden]]>><<run delete $avery_mansion.plant_together>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Mansion Garden Plant Together Kiss
<<set $location to "avery_mansion">><<set $bus to "avery_garden">><<set $outside to 0>><<effects>>
<<set _plant to setup.foodstuff[$avery_mansion.plant_together]>>
You step closer and kiss Avery. <<He>> stiffens in surprise, then places one hand against your waist and kisses you back.
When you start to pull away, <<his>> hand stays at your waist and <<he>> kisses you once more before letting you step back.
<br><br>
"Don't think this excuses you from watering them," <<he>> says, giving you a small smile.<<takeKissVirginity "Avery" `($auriga_artefact ? "loveInterest" : "romantic")`>>
<<npcincr Avery love 3>><<gglove>>
<br><br>
<span class="gold">You planted <<print _plant.name>> seeds with Avery.</span><<gtending>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Look over the plots|Mansion Garden Plots]]>><<run delete $avery_mansion.plant_together>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Leave|Mansion Garden]]>><<run delete $avery_mansion.plant_together>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Mansion Garden Plant Together Leave
<<set $location to "avery_mansion">><<set $bus to "avery_garden">><<set $outside to 0>><<effects>>
<<set _plant to setup.foodstuff[$avery_mansion.plant_together]>>
You stay beside Avery. <<He>> glances at you, then at the planted row, waiting for you to say something.
You leave the tools where they are instead of heading for the door. After a few seconds, <<he>> shifts closer until <<his>> shoulder rests against yours.
<br><br>
"This was pleasant," <<he>> says at last. "We should tend them together again."<<glove>><<npcincr Avery love 1>>
<br><br>
<span class="gold">You planted <<print _plant.name>> seeds with Avery.</span><<gtending>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Look over the plots|Mansion Garden Plots]]>><<run delete $avery_mansion.plant_together>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Leave|Mansion Garden]]>><<run delete $avery_mansion.plant_together>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>
